WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.780
Two essays on A Christmas Carol,
built paragraph by paragraph.

2
00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.700
The same four quotations drop into both.

3
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:11.780
This one, for a start:
"solitary as an oyster".

4
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:13.440
Both essays look neat.

5
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:17.320
Same length, same cards,
same number of paragraphs.

6
00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.940
Then the marks arrive.

7
00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.470
One essay scores double the other.

8
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.010
Same evidence, so what's different?

9
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:29.330
In this mission, you'll put the two essays
side by side and test the obvious answers.

10
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.190
Is the stronger one packed
with more technical terms?

11
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.240
Does it open with more history?

12
00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:38.050
And you'll rank opening statements
and sort topic sentences,

13
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.880
the way an examiner does.

14
00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.560
Your mission: work out why
one essay scores double.
